# QGC UI — landscape remote controllers first

When designing or implementing QGroundControl QML/UI in this workspace:

## Primary targets

Prefer **landscape handheld GCS remotes**, not phone-portrait layouts:

| Brand | Examples | Typical screen |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| **云卓 Skydroid** | G20 | 7″ ≈ 1920×1200 landscape (~960×600 dp) |
| **思翼 SIYI** | MK32, MK15 | 7″ / 5.5″ ≈ 1920×1080 landscape |

Height is usually the bottleneck (short landscape + Vehicle Setup sidebar). Desktop / tall phone portrait is secondary.

## Layout rules

- Default to **left/right split** (or otherwise keep primary controls in the first viewport) on short landscape.
- Do **not** assume tall stacked columns; a tall diagram alone will push controls off-screen.
- Prefer compact controls (`QGCSlider`, dense rows) over tall widgets (`ValueSlider`) on short screens.
- Use `ScreenTools.isShortScreen` / available height when choosing split vs stack.
- Touch targets must stay usable with gloves (`ScreenTools` / min touch sizing).

## Verification

After UI changes meant for Android remotes, check on (or simulate) a **short landscape** viewport — e.g. Skydroid G20 — not only desktop full screen.
